1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Carbon registries make sure a credit is retired only once.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,332
But a retirement is where the claims begin.

3
00:00:06,332 --> 00:00:14,154
Companies cite retired units in reports and product labels, often through brokers who split one retirement among many buyers.

4
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:19,574
If two claims cite the same units, each one looks fine on its own.

5
00:00:19,574 --> 00:00:25,822
And because they quote different serial strings in different documents, comparing hashes misses it.

6
00:00:27,102 --> 00:00:30,368
OnceOnly turns this into an investigation workflow.

7
00:00:30,368 --> 00:00:35,747
The registry records are real, from Berkeley's Voluntary Registry Offsets Database.

8
00:00:35,747 --> 00:00:37,925
The five companies are synthetic.

9
00:00:39,104 --> 00:00:43,525
Helios Apparel claims seven thousand units from a real Verra retirement.

10
00:00:43,525 --> 00:00:47,149
Each serial becomes an interval inside its registry batch.

11
00:00:48,334 --> 00:00:54,449
Four thousand, five hundred and fifty-nine of those units already back Northwind's anchored claim.

12
00:00:54,449 --> 00:00:58,943
When the registration was forced, the smart contract itself refused it.

13
00:01:00,117 --> 00:01:02,666
The reconciliation explains the overlap.

14
00:01:02,666 --> 00:01:13,630
It is classified as an allocation conflict between different entities: not a broker acting for a disclosed client, not a parent and subsidiary, and not a legitimate split.

15
00:01:13,630 --> 00:01:16,244
It ends with a next step, not a verdict.

16
00:01:17,426 --> 00:01:21,128
The assessment console applies sixteen deterministic rules.

17
00:01:21,128 --> 00:01:25,772
Each finding shows its metrics, its limitations and a recommended action.

18
00:01:25,772 --> 00:01:30,102
Correlated signals are grouped, so they cannot inflate the priority.

19
00:01:31,268 --> 00:01:34,064
Projects can appear on more than one registry.

20
00:01:34,064 --> 00:01:44,399
The cross-registry workspace ranks candidate Verra and Gold Standard pairs, and treats an identical project ID on two registries as a collision, never as the same asset.

21
00:01:45,566 --> 00:01:50,982
The observatory describes the population: thirty-seven thousand real retirements.

22
00:01:50,982 --> 00:01:55,663
Most name no beneficiary, which is a disclosure fact, not misconduct.

23
00:01:55,663 --> 00:01:59,275
Every population figure was reproduced independently.

24
00:02:00,461 --> 00:02:02,762
Finally, anyone can verify a claim.

25
00:02:02,762 --> 00:02:07,431
Northwind's original statement matches the commitment stored on chain.

26
00:02:08,619 --> 00:02:11,271
A copy with a single flipped bit does not.

27
00:02:11,271 --> 00:02:18,978
Each check is reported separately, and the network is stated plainly: a local development chain, not a public blockchain.

28
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:22,828
OnceOnly flags evidence for human review.

29
00:02:22,828 --> 00:02:28,554
It does not decide who is right, and its benchmarks are labelled for what they measure.

30
00:02:28,554 --> 00:02:30,832
Every retired tonne, claimed once.

